# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out as CRLF on Windows
# while the committed blobs stay LF, so the same file has different bytes on
# different machines. The content layer reads those bytes directly
# (`readFileSync` in src/lib/content/load.js), so a CRLF checkout can produce
# different rendered output than a Linux one.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the index on every platform, which is
# what Obsidian, VS Code, and git all handle without surprise. `text=auto`
# keeps git's own binary detection, so images and fonts are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
